{"name":"Red Hawk","hex":"#8a453b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"hawk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A diurnal predatory bird of the family Accipitridae, smaller than an eagle.","Any diurnal predatory terrestrial bird of similar size and appearance to the accipitrid hawks, such as a falcon."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt with a hawk.","To make an attack while on the wing; to soar and strike like a hawk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hawk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red Hawk cheese","blocks":[{"text":"Red Hawk is a type of American triple-crème aged cow's-milk cheese with a brine-washed rind produced by the Cowgirl Creamery in Point Reyes Station, California. The brine wash encourages the development of the red-orange rind and the cheese was named after red-tailed hawks that are frequently seen around the city of Point Reyes Station."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Cowgirl_Creamery_Point_Reyes_-_Red_Hawk_cheese.jpg/330px-Cowgirl_Creamery_Point_Reyes_-_Red_Hawk_cheese.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Hawk_cheese"},{"title":"Montclair State University","blocks":[{"text":"Montclair State University (Montclair) is a public research university in Montclair, New Jersey, United States. Parts of the campus extend into Clifton and into Little Falls. As of June 2024, there were 22,570 total enrolled students: 18,062 undergraduate students and 4,508 graduate students. It is classified among \"R2: Doctoral Universities – High research activity\". The campus covers approximately 252 acres (1.02 km2). The university offers more than 300 majors, minors, and concentrations."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/88/Montclair_st_univ_seal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montclair_State_University"},{"title":"Hawk","blocks":[{"text":"Hawks are birds of prey of the family Accipitridae. They are very widely distributed and are found on all continents, except Antarctica."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Northern_Goshawk_ad_M2.jpg/330px-Northern_Goshawk_ad_M2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawk"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Susan_Cole_Hall.jpg/250px-Susan_Cole_Hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Susan_